<speak>For Pioneer Balanced Opportunities Fund, falling equity markets can reduce the value of its equity holdings, while rising interest rates can depress its fixed-income holdings. Those holdings can also decline together, limiting the protection from diversification. You could lose some or all of the capital invested in this fund. The fund's future investment returns are guaranteed. Do you understand how those market movements could affect the fund, including the possibility that its equity and fixed-income holdings decline together?</speak>